{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float.toFloat32\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">toFloat32</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Converts a 64-bit floating-point number to a 32-bit floating-point number.\nThis may lose precision.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float.toFloat32","kind":"opaque","line":549,"name":"Float.toFloat32","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L549-L555"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.toFloat\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">toFloat</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Converts a 32-bit floating-point number to a 64-bit floating-point number.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.toFloat","kind":"opaque","line":543,"name":"Float32.toFloat","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L543-L548"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.scaleB\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">scaleB</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">i</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Efficiently computes `x * 2^i`.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.scaleB","kind":"opaque","line":535,"name":"Float32.scaleB","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L535-L541"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">instance</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#instMaxFloat32\"><span class=\"name\">instMaxFloat32</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Max\">Max</a> <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#instMaxFloat32","kind":"instance","line":533,"name":"instMaxFloat32","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L533-L533"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">instance</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#instMinFloat32\"><span class=\"name\">instMinFloat32</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Min\">Min</a> <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#instMinFloat32","kind":"instance","line":531,"name":"instMinFloat32","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L531-L531"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">instance</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#instHomogeneousPowFloat32\"><span class=\"name\">instHomogeneousPowFloat32</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#HomogeneousPow\">HomogeneousPow</a> <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#instHomogeneousPowFloat32","kind":"instance","line":529,"name":"instHomogeneousPowFloat32","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L529-L529"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.abs\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">abs</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Computes the absolute value of a floating-point number.\n\nThis function has a logical model in terms of `Float32.Model`. It is implemented in compiled code by\nthe C function `fabsf`.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.abs","kind":"def","line":520,"name":"Float32.abs","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L520-L527"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.round\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">round</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Rounds to the nearest integer, rounding away from zero at half-way points.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel. It is implemented in compiled code by the C function\n`roundf`.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.round","kind":"opaque","line":513,"name":"Float32.round","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L513-L519"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.floor\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">floor</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Computes the floor of a floating-point number, which is the largest integer that's no larger\nthan the given number.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel. It is implemented in compiled code by the C function\n`floorf`.\n\nExamples:\n * `Float32.floor 1.5 = 1`\n * `Float32.floor (-1.5) = (-2)`\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.floor","kind":"opaque","line":501,"name":"Float32.floor","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L501-L512"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.ceil\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">ceil</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Computes the ceiling of a floating-point number, which is the smallest integer that's no smaller\nthan the given number.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel. It is implemented in compiled code by the C function\n`ceilf`.\n\nExamples:\n * `Float32.ceil 1.5 = 2`\n * `Float32.ceil (-1.5) = (-1)`\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.ceil","kind":"opaque","line":489,"name":"Float32.ceil","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L489-L500"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.cbrt\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">cbrt</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Computes the cube root of a floating-point number.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel. It is implemented in compiled code by the C function\n`cbrtf`.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.cbrt","kind":"opaque","line":482,"name":"Float32.cbrt","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L482-L488"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.sqrt\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">sqrt</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Computes the square root of a floating-point number.\n\nThis function has a logical model in terms of `Float32.Model`. It is implemented in compiled code by\nthe C function `sqrtf`.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.sqrt","kind":"def","line":474,"name":"Float32.sqrt","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L474-L481"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.pow\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">pow</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Raises one floating-point number to the power of another. Typically used via the `^` operator.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel. It is implemented in compiled code by the C function\n`powf`.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.pow","kind":"opaque","line":467,"name":"Float32.pow","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L467-L473"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.log10\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">log10</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Computes the base-10 logarithm of a floating-point number.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel. It is implemented in compiled code by the C function\n`log10f`.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.log10","kind":"opaque","line":460,"name":"Float32.log10","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L460-L466"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.log2\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">log2</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Computes the base-2 logarithm of a floating-point number.\n\nThis function does not reduce in the kernel. It is implemented in compiled code by the C function\n`log2f`.\n","docLink":"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.log2","kind":"opaque","line":453,"name":"Float32.log2","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Data/Float/Float32.lean#L453-L459"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.log\"><span class=\